[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64ba57cc-a3eb-582a-963b-b94895a20bac" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points From Linear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5782671c-06f9-5f2b-be1b-47ecd68b0a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449826} {:answer/id #uuid "84c0a9e7-8b48-59b2-be51-a59ff96c1fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84c0a9e7-8b48-59b2-be51-a59ff96c1fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449827} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d7625d0-db05-5ac1-a27e-1e2fdb8985b3" :answer-field/key "The point $P(1,1)$ lies on the boundary of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450867} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a13ef65-ad91-5556-a28f-c5de9b2e025b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449828} {:answer/id #uuid "23ffc9c3-ea3d-5c39-82f6-923b77b6c6ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a13ef65-ad91-5556-a28f-c5de9b2e025b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449828} :answer-field/id #uuid "c70e0550-6f21-5cb8-8ed7-b230fc1f354c" :answer-field/key "The point $P(1,1)$ belongs to $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ddb187c-7917-5b25-a13d-e7534f38d713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449830} {:answer/id #uuid "7843a164-1844-518d-951f-e5d980edf8bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ddb187c-7917-5b25-a13d-e7534f38d713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449830} :answer-field/id #uuid "64a78755-2a8a-5e4d-9ee4-e2613b6dd629" :answer-field/key "The point $Q(0,0)$ is an interior point of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2253cfff-ee0a-5c15-93af-d26f561ec17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-158603" :question/problem "The set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:x>1\\},\\,∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:x=1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n\\{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta \\}\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $A$ consists of all points that lie to the right of the line $x=1.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/7d/7dc932c43ed153f4ac1832ca136f9035d879ea1f54e01c69e7a032b7a53d4940.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(1,1)$ and $Q(0,0)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/06/06fdba4e26ebad28ef3f63106b7bdd8cb115b91a5f0076370a27b12f05added3.png)\n\n \n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The point $P(1,1)$ lies on the boundary of $A$” is true. The coordinates of $P(1,1)$ satisfy $x=1.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $∂A,$ the boundary of $A.$\n\n- Statement “The point $P(1,1)$ belongs to $A$” is false. The coordinates of $P(1,1)$ do not satisfy the inequality $x>1.$ Hence, $P$ does not lie in the set $A.$\n\n- Statement “The point $Q(0,0)$ is an interior point of $A$” is false. Indeed, $Q$ is not an interior point of $A$ since any neighborhood of $Q$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“The point $P(1,1)$ lies on the boundary of $A$” only.'"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34c9c06-e884-5758-a184-39330a07d8cd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points of Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c6e0563-60fe-573a-be2b-c09286e0d28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464600} {:answer/id #uuid "8e161fc7-1d15-5bde-b789-e5538def14f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e161fc7-1d15-5bde-b789-e5538def14f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464601} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed0c0536-5566-58ba-9627-1a27b29de0e8" :answer-field/key "$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82cac744-5325-5785-87eb-888aa14491a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464602} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf113b9-f90e-5668-ae93-83231d949649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaf113b9-f90e-5668-ae93-83231d949649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464603} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd29ecd-65da-5acc-9237-ce8e9eac3252" :answer-field/key "$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce6d1aa5-a903-545d-8b95-75b53ca2b13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464604} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f38a1c-72a0-5e6b-9320-c6e45960b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7f38a1c-72a0-5e6b-9320-c6e45960b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464605} :answer-field/id #uuid "001728ff-5f50-5db0-b0d4-7cdfa3b9596d" :answer-field/key "$C$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed33ac2f-6299-5342-b520-1399b2a77786" :question/math-academy-id "q-158684" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5dccdb1f8957bb15d7b2215320c6e632819a647bf4dc350ff850876bae6298ec.png)\n\nConsider the set $M=(-3,2]$ and the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}\\in R$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is *smaller than* $\\delta :$ \n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nA neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is given by the open interval $({x}_{0}-\\delta ,{x}_{0}+\\delta ),$ shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f889352f25e7936d0e5ea76585a979efbb301da61f7e99a937e979af93ee0664.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is true. The point $A$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $A$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n![](images/d5/d595e29d31743694c404b99c79c60e40b152d30083e633d4269ad4444be3f826.png)\n\n- Statement “$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is true. The point $B$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $B$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n![](images/23/2336ff8a65dd397e8324384b9f9536f3c7d4ad2d76a81caeba28d7fe3ec229ef.png)\n\n- Statement “$C$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is true. The point $C$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $C$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\n![](images/26/26903667d45cecf81539025c4cda333129cf89600821b383f20d574c75e537b0.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$”, “$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$”, and “$C$ is an interior point of the set $M$”.'"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34c9c06-e884-5758-a184-39330a07d8cd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points of Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96356f47-c178-5a33-bb0a-25787d54b790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464606} {:answer/id #uuid "d261f82c-07fe-537e-a6d4-ea593eb568c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d261f82c-07fe-537e-a6d4-ea593eb568c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464607} :answer-field/id #uuid "be11caff-d2e8-5f49-9988-c418cfadb534" :answer-field/key "$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae5e3317-6cb6-5f5d-8f8d-a588ac041b89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464608} {:answer/id #uuid "3edad2c7-dffb-510f-b03c-c40ad14a1dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae5e3317-6cb6-5f5d-8f8d-a588ac041b89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464608} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3d15ba-67d5-501c-b3be-022701568e8c" :answer-field/key "$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c485ad6-9c4f-5370-b143-0ce473c05f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464610} {:answer/id #uuid "e530432f-f73f-5284-bec5-159f1f6c1026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e530432f-f73f-5284-bec5-159f1f6c1026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464611} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1229fa5-9182-533b-9908-fc72ca3ea300" :answer-field/key "$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1861489-bfb5-5c9b-ba84-97990e733cb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-158685" :question/problem "![](images/73/73f61de1a716545449439ed8875b465dc5aec6f3148e520ad028a96725f2a4f0.png)\n\nConsider the set $M=[0,1]\\cup {2}$ and the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}\\in R$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is *smaller than* $\\delta :$ \n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nA neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is given by the open interval $({x}_{0}-\\delta ,{x}_{0}+\\delta ),$ shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f889352f25e7936d0e5ea76585a979efbb301da61f7e99a937e979af93ee0664.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is true. The point $A$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $A$ that is fully contained in the set $M.$\n\n![](images/84/84afb5331ef9244120d9f3d9b14e25fa2d19da31f8eb685c5d74b089e0d99289.png)\n\n- Statement “$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is false. The point $B$ is *not* an interior point of $M$ since any neighborhood of $B$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\n![](images/c0/c0b35fafc6e628c36e41fa8df42e3a477d8aac4af0b4c3819fa0063e5bd014df.png)\n\n- Statement “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is true. The point $C$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $C$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$ Notice that $C$ is a point of $M$ and $C$ belongs to any open neighborhood of $C.$\n\n![](images/e5/e54fa85543a79c18e00d3b03281d6774c98fdb03e9b5440b8f179ce5a0d09519.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$” and “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” only.'"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "24b9af85-3717-59e0-aa72-d701f3c6b6a8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points From Nonlinear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a80dd0f-0c82-561c-8d99-dbc60a866caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449832} {:answer/id #uuid "282bdddf-810b-5c46-b1f4-a4d97d1ad8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "282bdddf-810b-5c46-b1f4-a4d97d1ad8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449833} :answer-field/id #uuid "52e05642-c706-5c94-a220-76dc8f029d08" :answer-field/key "The point $P(-2,2)$ lies on the boundary of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "228181b3-f9ff-50e3-9654-b561905a1c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449834} {:answer/id #uuid "a717b966-f9cd-5be7-bc77-91f617d72c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a717b966-f9cd-5be7-bc77-91f617d72c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449835} :answer-field/id #uuid "93d2b24e-f77e-5937-ae54-d0bfd7ad911e" :answer-field/key "The point $P(-2,2)$ belongs to $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a040e126-a858-5b73-a230-f4ef9fe98f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449836} {:answer/id #uuid "5e002088-0b51-5625-aac8-dce1db05fd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a040e126-a858-5b73-a230-f4ef9fe98f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449836} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9c8be66-3b64-5a6c-ae03-ae585af86b31" :answer-field/key "The point $Q(-1,0)$ is an interior point of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98673ae2-3448-5c6b-87b7-226f4a36e93c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158731" :question/problem "The set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are given by\n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:{y}^{2}\\ge -2x},\\,∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:{y}^{2}=-2x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nThe set $A$ consists of all points that lie on or to the right of the parabola ${y}^{2}=-2x.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/e5/e5547cb8e0ed0fec1fd2e515a1bcd9009044289dfdc516c6a6cba14b650a7645.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(-2,2)$ and $Q(-1,0)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/7b/7b353dd43fd293424ba8404184e53869d41d8a1b73493d845bc85aa333130606.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The point $P(-2,2)$ lies on the boundary of $A$” is true. The coordinates of $P(-2,2)$ satisfy the equation ${y}^{2}=-2x.$ Hence, $P$ lies on the boundary of the set.\n\n- Statement “The point $P(-2,2)$ belongs to $A$” is true. The coordinates of $P(-2,2)$ satisfy the inequality ${y}^{2}\\ge -2x.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $A.$\n\n- Statement “The point $Q(-1,0)$ is an interior point of $A$” is false. Indeed, $Q$ is not an interior point of $A$ since any neighborhood of $Q$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“The point $P(-2,2)$ lies on the boundary of $A$” and “The point $P(-2,2)$ belongs to $A$” only.'"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "24b9af85-3717-59e0-aa72-d701f3c6b6a8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points From Nonlinear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deee2b7e-a408-581b-a336-ae5a067cb7d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449838} {:answer/id #uuid "9ffbb325-7c8e-5480-a009-16fc1b2a59c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deee2b7e-a408-581b-a336-ae5a067cb7d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449838} :answer-field/id #uuid "559da60d-836f-5f06-a5a8-0f303d82c83c" :answer-field/key "The point $P(1,2)$ lies on the boundary of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450873} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf3feed0-87bd-57d5-bef4-234195fb4d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449840} {:answer/id #uuid "1e449ed9-a64d-5bd6-8051-48d2b124afef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e449ed9-a64d-5bd6-8051-48d2b124afef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449841} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa396de4-6228-5edd-bcef-29063dd5a46e" :answer-field/key "The point $P(1,2)$ belongs to $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450874} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1c445d6-57f7-5242-8d1f-8af17ce0add6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449842} {:answer/id #uuid "61e9bb73-6a9c-5d88-befb-f38396d65cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1c445d6-57f7-5242-8d1f-8af17ce0add6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449842} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdb4e49e-b0a9-58fa-9d48-050b37aebebc" :answer-field/key "The point $Q(3,3)$ is an interior point of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6d4676b-36dc-5235-80c5-02c2a6d333fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-158733" :question/problem "The set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<9\\},\\,∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n\\{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta \\}\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $A$ consists of all points that lie inside the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/18/181a21e9975320e54365ef10bd801a2fa6494058dd40cda79cb29b713bd8df84.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(1,2)$ and $Q(3,3)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/15/15d42de861a3e687a269326e8338ea5d99b6a5a609f4a20e597e64ccc4a8474a.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The point $P(1,2)$ lies on the boundary of $A$” is false. The coordinates of $P(1,2)$ do not satisfy the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.$ Hence, $P$ does not lie in the set $∂A,$ the boundary of $A.$\n\n- Statement “The point $P(1,2)$ belongs to $A$” is true. The coordinates of $P(1,2)$ satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<9.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $A.$\n\n- Statement “The point $Q(3,3)$ is an interior point of $A$” is false. Indeed, $Q$ is not an interior point of $A$ since any neighborhood of $Q$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“The point $P(1,2)$ belongs to $A$” only'."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34c9c06-e884-5758-a184-39330a07d8cd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points of Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da84b591-c069-52ac-9c33-3cbe81429ac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464612} {:answer/id #uuid "120918e2-eb16-5fa6-9adb-45f664ff0083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da84b591-c069-52ac-9c33-3cbe81429ac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464612} :answer-field/id #uuid "75cf6afa-715a-5ca0-b81d-77031bf4f69a" :answer-field/key "$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465240} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b920332-7ab9-53f5-a66f-7e6e5e235621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464614} {:answer/id #uuid "b4762625-68f0-540b-a385-073f5149badc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b920332-7ab9-53f5-a66f-7e6e5e235621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464614} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1cbe44f-f573-547b-af11-201b5753cc7c" :answer-field/key "$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7f916f3-5685-5163-bb92-295d29d3e52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464616} {:answer/id #uuid "ee73bdb3-7ab9-52f5-aa5c-7e2e6cf63727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee73bdb3-7ab9-52f5-aa5c-7e2e6cf63727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464617} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c34efb7-eb3f-5e3d-86d5-583c5f0a2247" :answer-field/key "$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94c1ba54-750c-5dd8-b08c-c465652d3c9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-159264" :question/problem "![](images/07/07463b409d54d1970ee9d47cad5de7188ea44e682a58e7e941b3cd4bf7f5efa6.png)\n\nConsider the set $M=(-1,1)$ and the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}\\in R$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is *smaller than* $\\delta :$ \n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nA neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is given by the open interval $({x}_{0}-\\delta ,{x}_{0}+\\delta ),$ shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f889352f25e7936d0e5ea76585a979efbb301da61f7e99a937e979af93ee0664.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is false. The point $A$ is *not* a boundary point since there exists an open neighborhood of $A$ that is fully contained inside $M.$\n\n![](images/73/734ff08a25e25486dc65f919ce99bc5422ca8ce264bb7d044479b1eb3b6a716b.png)\n\n- Statement “$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is false. The point $B$ is *not* an interior point of $M$ since any neighborhood of $B$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\n![](images/28/286f8b397b3c908d29678640d691558a784e31751d09c68e6b6da855c272231c.png)\n\n- Statement “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is true. The point $C$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $C$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n![](images/7e/7ed7726fa1a139ded4a9226bcb01c17d0ad46ef4bd03a820f033640c68778453.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” only.'"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34c9c06-e884-5758-a184-39330a07d8cd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points of Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "965d6742-d43d-5b49-a4a9-cd548fdadd01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464618} {:answer/id #uuid "4e048152-f58e-59b3-b44b-f6cd0d6203ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e048152-f58e-59b3-b44b-f6cd0d6203ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464619} :answer-field/id #uuid "afe690a6-055a-56f6-b52f-80b5076dafd9" :answer-field/key "$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adce2641-9123-56f3-ba1a-924970eada55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464620} {:answer/id #uuid "018531bc-f41f-504c-b659-c346c1c579cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adce2641-9123-56f3-ba1a-924970eada55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464620} :answer-field/id #uuid "73be4277-75bd-5ce4-ba2f-74f90bbbf40c" :answer-field/key "$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "887cea53-b99a-57d0-9e36-5eeb47cf6d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464622} {:answer/id #uuid "fe32bb85-f55a-532f-8e2d-65abbf3459df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "887cea53-b99a-57d0-9e36-5eeb47cf6d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464622} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff6f08d-fa55-559f-b858-e2ad4a1fa773" :answer-field/key "$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae427c1b-c208-5c4a-a164-5e046d8d2ea3" :question/math-academy-id "q-159274" :question/problem "![](images/43/43380e1382df5db66c4a9ab0ee385e98073da7fb684ccdf93a665e223fb1a554.png)\n\nConsider the set $M=(-\\infty ,1)$ and the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}\\in R$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is *smaller than* $\\delta :$ \n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nA neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is given by the open interval $({x}_{0}-\\delta ,{x}_{0}+\\delta ),$ shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f889352f25e7936d0e5ea76585a979efbb301da61f7e99a937e979af93ee0664.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is true. The point $A$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $A$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\n![](images/c6/c66edbc427dbd1e970a5c25422fbfca39296b0a90b6ca26dacb3280551105784.png)\n\n- Statement “$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is false. The point $B$ is *not* an interior point of $M$ since any neighborhood of $B$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\n![](images/7b/7b8beea4c575e89b2c66f363271a90068e912422ad8991a333375f6894523a57.png)\n\n- Statement “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is false. The point $C$ is *not* a boundary point since there exists any neighborhood of $C$ that is fully contained *outside* the set $M.$\n\n![](images/4a/4a06851f25bf80edcc934fe7f341a6a43a065e744691164d46f77d116d4bf047.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$” only.'"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69b456ea-44de-59f0-b2c8-bc5b9495974f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f30f8006-242d-5815-b4e6-55180636d13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464624} {:answer/id #uuid "ef125b16-49f4-57ed-a235-602a4af9bf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef125b16-49f4-57ed-a235-602a4af9bf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464625} :answer-field/id #uuid "614ca28a-51fa-5e6b-824d-0455718a1caf" :answer-field/key "$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "743ea134-bede-5e5d-85c1-b8959c98fb2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464626} {:answer/id #uuid "eee1c213-a5e6-5182-adec-568d9d22a6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eee1c213-a5e6-5182-adec-568d9d22a6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464627} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe6e976a-ce43-535a-834b-e62cc2342a63" :answer-field/key "$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddd57b68-0ced-5792-aded-4f16279eb1ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464628} {:answer/id #uuid "8d462a0f-93c1-5775-84c1-96d61ea828a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddd57b68-0ced-5792-aded-4f16279eb1ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464628} :answer-field/id #uuid "d83acde9-9dda-58e0-a072-e702efca6af3" :answer-field/key "$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "951baf6c-974c-552a-a084-e87ba6cba5d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-159485" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f4ad8b759d3f2781b1dc6adf64e58a230218655249f21fdd8f6a852568554ead.png)\n\nConsider the set $M,$ depicted by the shaded region above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/56/56a640baf27e1acb5c3428e1bef25a87b3ff965dff71762b94fb1eff94aaf24d.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is true. Indeed, $A$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $A$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n- Statement “$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is true. Indeed, $B$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $B$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\n- Statement “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is false. The point $C$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $C$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“$A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” and “$B$ is an interior point of the set $M$” only'."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69b456ea-44de-59f0-b2c8-bc5b9495974f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f560f963-41fb-5961-a4ca-e7f4fae76b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464630} {:answer/id #uuid "49e308bf-0f02-5eb9-b2bc-bf86afa295d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f560f963-41fb-5961-a4ca-e7f4fae76b45" :answer/