 above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=2{e}^{1-2x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }2{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-2x}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is false. Since statement ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d91c88-80cf-5e60-9a02-2f8a1add5d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449856} {:answer/id #uuid "c443fbcc-7008-5fcc-8677-7121e62ef09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c443fbcc-7008-5fcc-8677-7121e62ef09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449857} :answer-field/id #uuid "b59689df-fb76-51e8-9daf-ad4252596a48" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fa2b70-fac9-5247-a29a-0d350830d9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449858} {:answer/id #uuid "6f690e9b-7ffc-5ad5-83ae-6a067ff174c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f690e9b-7ffc-5ad5-83ae-6a067ff174c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449859} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f06dc6-aaa0-54c5-8f15-50401effd928" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "992aa33e-1dc4-5291-be9f-c6c9fdfa3acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449860} {:answer/id #uuid "d25be699-e60e-5b9d-8d86-f00138ba80a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25be699-e60e-5b9d-8d86-f00138ba80a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449861} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab69c169-9c3c-5352-a088-046eca05101b" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e574537-84e0-52ce-b8da-3afe1320a385" :question/math-academy-id "q-160459" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is true. Since statements “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$” and ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$”; ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$; “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5b2ba9-1bfe-57b5-9caf-c99e7cd00766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465315} {:answer/id #uuid "0e47c71f-651b-5dab-adbd-31cee6b0d544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a5b2ba9-1bfe-57b5-9caf-c99e7cd00766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465315} :answer-field/id #uuid "81d1cd43-a1b8-500d-ac08-e5f0fb4d4fe8" :answer-field/key "The point $(1,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96cce611-53f4-585e-abe8-9b124fe8324e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465317} {:answer/id #uuid "6aae8e41-20a4-5fa6-a286-626b3ae6f630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aae8e41-20a4-5fa6-a286-626b3ae6f630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465318} :answer-field/id #uuid "b37cfc2c-cedf-5629-9c08-1c82f0317e43" :answer-field/key "The point $(1,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8081da32-5615-591d-a668-9527b67107cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465319} {:answer/id #uuid "7537192a-f28a-5528-8449-0c72e08da197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8081da32-5615-591d-a668-9527b67107cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465319} :answer-field/id #uuid "14279bd7-1c43-5024-8057-80e3b4ec2a59" :answer-field/key "The point $(-1,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61d3fab2-038b-5d24-9a0c-708feb5787d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160617" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,1),(-1,2),(1,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is the same as counterclockwise rotation by the same angle. It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,-1),(1,-2),(-1,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(1,-2)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12754a27-cfb2-59a0-a8a9-3ab89e93f58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/iden