s boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 8,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{x}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70c6d476-7089-554f-a53f-d0eeffbcff46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465435} {:answer/id #uuid "e2df68f7-1103-5962-9b9f-e16827511e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2df68f7-1103-5962-9b9f-e16827511e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465436} :answer-field/id #uuid "349c0ef9-a03e-5c46-a30f-56ab22eb74e8" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}\\le 1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e373ead-fb73-58f1-9916-cc8fdec6aebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :