wer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c52a783-530c-5154-a072-ed464f679923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465476} :answer-field/id #uuid "a17b70a5-9aa2-55e8-b7fb-0e4865faf9bb" :answer-field/key "The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=0$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8eff559e-2582-52e2-ae0e-c082d3e9afb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161866" :question/problem "![](images/67/675226780bb9627524f4ab03691e84e312300f398f352abc3b698c1fcdd83490.png)\n\nThe function $f(x),$ whose graph is shown above, has a stationary point at $x=-1$ and is continuously differentiable everywhere except at $x=0.$  By considering the points indicated in the diagram, determine which of the following statements **must** be true according to the inverse function theorem.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=0$” is false. Notice that $f$ is not continuous at $x=0.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\n- Statement “${f}^{-1}(y)$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $y=1$” is also false. Notice that $y=1=f(-1).$  However, the function $f$ does *not* satisfy the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=-1$ since ${f}^{′}(-1)=0.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\n- Statement “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=0$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)}$” is true. Notice that $y=0=f(2),$ and the function $f$ satisfies the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=2.$ Indeed,\n\n- $f$ is continuously differentiable on an open set containing $x=2,$ for example, $(1,3),$ and\n\n- the derivative of $f$ is nonzero at $x=2,$ i.e., ${f}^{′}(2)\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, by the inverse function theorem, the derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=0$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=0$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d65d348-380b-5f1a-8d6d-4fe1b2db6b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449988} {:answer/id #uuid "59c93832-fe98-545b-859c-ae8eb173bd4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d65d348-380b-5f1a-8d6d-4fe1b2db6b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449988} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dd1bf69-489b-5265-9fa9-4746d265dca2" :answer-field/key "${w}^{4}+1=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc47b583-9334-5b64-b2a1-d1741b28cf8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449990} {:answer/id #uuid "fe392d18-15aa-5a5b-9916-5395ad1e6647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe392d18-15aa-5a5b-9916-5395ad1e6647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449991} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0d3092d-28e8-5f0f-8af6-41deece82164" :answer-field/key "${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450949} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c096ebcf-8397-5faf-9dd6-c2509fd106b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449992} {:answer/id #uuid "655d1d09-5adb-5ec9-b4bd-060d64f54341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "655d1d09-5adb-5ec9-b4bd-060d64f54341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449993} :answer-field/id #uuid "bddffa24-0649-52c9-a5aa-e2628f8f7a10" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46fbce01-7db5-5630-8364-44d4a151bbf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-162346" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $4$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement ${w}^{4}+1=1$ is false. If $z$ and $w$ are $4$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{4}={w}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n{w}^{4}+1=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Statement ${\\left(\\frac{z}{w}\\right)}^{4}=1$ is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{z}{w}\\right)}^{4} & =\\frac{{z}^{4}}{{w}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity” is true. From statement ${\\left(\\frac{z}{w}\\right)}^{4}=1$, we have that ${\\left(\\frac{z}{w}\\right)}^{4}=1,$ which means that $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the quotient of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\left(\\frac{z}{w}\\right)}^{4}=1$; “$\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d21fd0f3-61ca-55b8-992d-8caa336fbfe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449994} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3cb37a-0a0d-5ba0-8686-df40ab573c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d21fd0f3-61ca-55b8-992d-8caa336fbfe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449994} :answer-field/id #uuid "1310c1aa-028f-5307-8a9b-23867e91afa4" :answer-field/key "$({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae485c08-a054-506e-b702-e021a9033658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449996} {:answer/id #uuid "5977334f-6d05-5c75-ab12-d528d65f25ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5977334f-6d05-5c75-ab12-d528d65f25ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449997} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cbb280b-5ca4-53e4-8eac-de7da419020a" :answer-field/key "${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6707a3db-6596-5e6d-9281-5b095bdf34a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449998} {:answer/id #uuid "19b1a7f5-a6d2-5a80-808e-8390fc639dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19b1a7f5-a6d2-5a80-808e-8390fc639dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449999} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d8aaf5-f0f6-51e8-a03e-90aeb065f7a7" :answer-field/key "${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b77c81df-773f-534f-b1e3-2174eb2531c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-162347" :question/problem "Let $z$ be a $6$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$ is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{2}={z}^{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity” is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{6} & =({z}^{6})^{3} \\\\  & =(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement “${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity” is true. From statement $({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{3})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity”; “${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cba55a4b-f247-535c-9e49-fa2e8c2cdcdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450000} {:answer/id #uuid "e93d1625-d6c8-5fd7-b1f4-1422b448e402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e93d1625-d6c8-5fd7-b1f4-1422b448e402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450001} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f940e62-9613-5985-ad24-d69a320fcd23" :answer-field/key "${z}^{8}=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9838a96-9d28-5e6e-86ab-1e2df5d2dd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450002} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f9dfb2-aace-5204-aa68-9a6d39b1025b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f9dfb2-aace-5204-aa68-9a6d39b1025b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450003} :answer-field/id #uuid "45127e67-9050-53d7-aa37-4528a5b9d664" :answer-field/key "$(zw)^{8}=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "958ca900-dd33-56fd-ae4b-202ef4468f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450004} {:answer/id #uuid "cca75b27-9e73-5231-8841-30d90c37c9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cca75b27-9e73-5231-8841-30d90c37c9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450005} :answer-field/id #uuid "4631cdd6-da5c-5378-87e3-d81dc85b8e48" :answer-field/key "$zw$ is an $8$th root of unity" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b299b05-4c26-5412-a581-f913a340d791" :question/math-academy-id "q-162348" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $8$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement ${z}^{8}=1$ is true. Indeed, if $z$ and $w$ are $8$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{8}={w}^{8}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement $(zw)^{8}=1$ is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{8} & ={z}^{8}{w}^{8} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$zw$ is an $8$th root of unity” is true. From statement $(zw)^{8}=1$, we have that $(zw)^{8}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is an $8$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${z}^{8}=1$; $(zw)^{8}=1$; “$zw$ is an $8$th root of unity”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed9a3736-62df-50c7-b100-037983515653" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450006} {:answer/id #uuid "30ec1f10-0f13-5ab1-b78e-da8de5ca4523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed9a3736-62df-50c7-b100-037983515653" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450006} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd66dc7d-be09-5eab-b0c3-11b236001c21" :answer-field/key "$({z}^{4})^{2}=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cc9f196-19e3-5b46-9f8e-dcf8ef6de5b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450008} {:answer/id #uuid "1a34f3c0-90de-50c7-abea-1d9cab231c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a34f3c0-90de-50c7-abea-1d9cab231c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450009} :answer-field/id #uuid "cad973f3-2202-53ec-8a04-d6d3d4934ea2" :answer-field/key "${z}^{4}$ is an $8$th root of unity" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450958} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6daa1574-cefd-5fca-8a27-09333b61c987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450010} {:answer/id #uuid "41fda86a-2906-564e-874d-326e526da153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41fda86a-2906-564e-874d-326e526da153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450011} :answer-field/id #uuid "facbe088-cd3d-5c74-a75a-2f688e42e0fd" :answer-field/key "${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4a65d62e-3083-571b-b429-c51c7b117795" :question/math-academy-id "q-162349" :question/problem "Let $z$ be an $8$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $({z}^{4})^{2}=-1$ is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({z}^{4})}^{2}={z}^{8}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${z}^{4}$ is an $8$th root of unity” is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{4})^{8} & =({z}^{8})^{4} \\\\  & =(1)^{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{4}$ is a $8$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement “${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity” is true. From statement $({z}^{4})^{2}=-1$, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{4})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${z}^{4}$ is an $8$th root of unity”; “${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8098262b-8dd2-5624-9085-904625cfb887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450012} {:answer/id #uuid "565d1fea-c5a2-50c4-8fb6-b49214d1efd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8098262b-8dd2-5624-9085-904625cfb887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450012} :answer-field/id #uuid "018e94fa-5c72-5d74-bab6-124b7efe13f3" :answer-field/key "${z}^{4}=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc737ac-0b5f-5ac2-afd0-362038549581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450014} {:answer/id #uuid "9ffcc792-724b-59e1-af60-c0c0de877e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cc737ac-0b5f-5ac2-afd0-362038549581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450014} :answer-field/id #uuid "582b02fd-0bcc-529d-8