id #edb/ref 17592186450034} :answer-field/id #uuid "cac92ed1-bc20-55bc-9a9a-5a514bc44b7a" :answer-field/key "$zw$ is not a $6$th root of unity" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b7bc6df-b3cb-50da-83fc-955ab52a05f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-162369" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $6$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $z{w}^{6}=w$ is false. Indeed,  since $z$ and $w$ are $6$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have\n\n$$\n{z}^{6}={w}^{6}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\nz{w}^{6}=z\\cdot 1=z\\ne w.\n$$\n\n- Statement $(zw)^{6}=1$ is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{6} & ={z}^{6}{w}^{6} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$zw$ is not a $6$th root of unity” is false. We have seen above that $(zw)^{6}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is a $6$th root of unity.  \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(zw)^{6}=1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7c2d70-ba75-5ef8-9097-90bddc50b4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450036} {:answer/id #uuid "8120d27e-6b2e-5bc7-b0d7-67a8bde31356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c7c2d70-ba75-5ef8-9097-90bddc50b4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450036} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e48cef-ad68-54f9-ba61-c315918da173" :answer-field/key "$p(x)\\in N,$ where $p(x)={x}^{3}-1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "983c66ff-c84d-5db7-a81a-8e7b44a5fd0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450038} {:answer/id #uuid "99dcf27d-c822-58ad-ae4e-86be30e29f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99dcf27d-c822-58ad-ae4e-86be30e29f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450039} :answer-field/id #uuid "200056d3-b737-545d-a891-be7f2e1df5b6" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450973} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f724c9d-ed07-57ad-b98a-93fd792e8837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450040} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d9d07f-d563-5a25-967e-56613d363fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7d9d07f-d563-5a25-967e-56613d363fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450041} :answer-field/id #uuid "9536bd2c-2cb7-5126-9d02-c69eb4ee5a13" :answer-field/key "The set is closed under addition." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62a3796-3a93-54ec-8c55-9e54ca670215" :question/math-academy-id "q-162379" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement “$p(x)\\in N,$ where $p(x)={x}^{3}-1.$” is false. We have, $p(x)={x}^{3}-1\\notin N$ because\n\n$$\np(0)=(0)^{3}-1=-1\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$” is true. Indeed, suppose $f(x),g(x)\\in N,$ where $f(0)=0$ and $g(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nf(0)+g(0)=0+0=0.\n$$\n\nHence $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$\n\n- Statement “The set is closed under addition” is true. Since statement “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$” is true, the set is closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$”; “The set is closed under addition” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baecaaf6-adc1-5d33-8bb8-faa4d72e9b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450042} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6d539e-41ec-53a4-a51e-3ac27752733a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baecaaf6-adc1-5d33-8bb8-faa4d72e9b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450042} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0a6dde1-6915-5386-9e54-09f03885a256" :answer-field/key "The  matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $S.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4841091b-2e64-5984-821c-cc3100911960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450044} {:answer/id #uuid "4714431a-4c69-5d40-b0eb-f99202ac6ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4714431a-4c69-5d40-b0eb-f99202ac6ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450045} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef2520d6-e623-58d6-b7c6-97e729a08a49" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e9b0ff-d627-5567-9969-d7cee3aac65b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450046} {:answer/id #uuid "b20b3572-1110-5d75-a050-ca0b765e2ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b20b3572-1110-5d75-a050-ca0b765e2ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450047} :answer-field/id #uuid "451e24a9-762f-57f2-bbfd-3d7dbb6ae449" :answer-field/key "For any $A,B,C\\in S,$ we have $A+(B-C)=(A+B)-C.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9060a6c-635e-5bea-91ee-1f014ee29783" :question/math-academy-id "q-162391" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant different from $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The  matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $S.$” is false. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$” is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with real entries,   there is a corresponding negative matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice if $A\\in S$ then \n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot |A|=|A|\\ne 0,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in S.$\n\n- Statement “For any $A,B,C\\in S,$ we have $A+(B-C)=(A+B)-C.$” is true. Indeed, for any matrices $A,B\\in S,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nA+(B-C)=A+(B+(-C))=(A+B)+(-C)=(A+B)-C\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$”; “For any $A,B,C\\in S,$ we have $A+(B-C)=(A+B)-C.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30bb7b96-0ee1-540e-a86d-287f27a702b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450048} {:answer/id #uuid "37ffb9ee-3671-538d-82eb-1a76ca7b6bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37ffb9ee-3671-538d-82eb-1a76ca7b6bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450049} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e2d51bd-2585-5f79-94d3-b038a415082e" :answer-field/key "The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b0a5de1-ebdf-50db-b852-bdb9ce68a858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450050} {:answer/id #uuid "a60f5a43-04d9-5f88-b2bc-365bc6d9531d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b0a5de1-ebdf-50db-b852-bdb9ce68a858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450050} :answer-field/id #uuid "196f729e-b1a5-5503-a13d-a4964e7a82dd" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)-q(x)=q(x)-p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450979} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1997ce5d-b934-50cb-856c-b4aaa92fef20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450052} {:answer/id #uuid "a552e5a8-222c-522a-b522-815b9887824d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1997ce5d-b934-50cb-856c-b4aaa92fef20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450052} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6507d2c-9d83-5368-870c-3233d9d50c59" :answer-field/key "There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)$ $\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b2f6345-ac14-55a4-a687-5a14893fcf90" :question/math-academy-id "q-162392" :question/problem "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2},$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$” is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as \n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot {x}^{3}+0\\cdot {x}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \nHence, $0\\in U.$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)-q(x)=q(x)-p(x).$” is false. For example, consider the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{3}\\in U$ and the zero-polynomial $q(x)=0\\in U.$ Then \n\n$$\np(x)-q(x)=p(x)-0={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nwhile \n\n$$\nq(x)-p(x)=0-p(x)=-{x}^{3}\\ne {x}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)$ $\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$” is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have \n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)],\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1934f404-12fe-5061-8332-ddf77cb3358c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450054} {:answer/id #uuid "74f484ed-f46c-525a-91d9-9aaef9742b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1934f404-12fe-5061-8332-ddf77cb3358c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450054} :answer-field/id #uuid "3459f397-effb-554b-8666-6e19befcd06c" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=\\sqrt{2y}$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af42c2a-0086-5f9d-b466-8f7cf82f0afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450056} {:answer/id #uuid "b8443a5b-debf-548f-b22a-c7ad859d5840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8443a5b-debf-548f-b22a-c7ad859d5840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450057} :answer-field/id #uuid "e741088c-ec60-5745-a82c-5940206acaae" :answer-field/key "${g}_{1}(y)=-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$ and ${g}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5820bb4-4dd8-5a96-b849-4c1a4fe09b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450058} {:answer/id #uuid "d9479a5c-4388-57b2-95d8-85f7d1fd0876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5820bb4-4dd8-5a96-b849-4c1a4fe09b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450058} :answer-field/id #uuid "23ec5b6c-64cb-56f5-9f54-68b907247bdd" :answer-field/key "$a=-1$ and $b=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b6ba3e9-8414-5dea-8a72-007f56c21b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162530" :question/problem "The region $R$ is bounded between the cone $x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ and the paraboloid $x=\\sqrt{2y}.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,{g}_{1}(y)\\le z\\le {g}_{2}(y),\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional region of type II can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nLet's find a type II representation of our region.\n\n**Step 1.** We start by finding the surfaces ${f}_{1}(y,z)$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z).$ Since all $x$ in the region are bounded *below* by $x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ and *above* by $x=\\sqrt{2y},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}_{{f}_{1}(y,z)}\\le x\\le \\underbrace{\\sqrt{2y}}_{{f}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nSo, statement “${f}_{1}(y,z)=\\sqrt{2y}$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$” is false.\n\n**Step 2.** We find the projection of the intersection between the cone $x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ and the paraboloid $x=\\sqrt{2y}$ onto the $yz$-plane.\n\nNotice that the equation of the cone is already solved for $x.$ Substituting this expression for $x$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{2y} \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =2y \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y+{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y+1+{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the projection of the intersection is the circle $(y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ centered at $(1,0)$ in the $yz$-plane. \n\n![](images/d6/d6db5f2d27787c5414f92c2525398b3810d0b0d192ea6837f7cdf483531f48e9.png)\n\nThe region is bounded *below* by $z=-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$ and bounded *above* by $z=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}_{{g}_{1}(y)}\\le z\\le \\underbrace{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}_{{g}_{2}(y)}.\n$$\n\nSo, statement “${g}_{1}(y)=-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$ and ${g}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$” is true.\n\n**Step 3.** We find the bounds for $y.$ From the diagram, $y$ is bounded *below* by $y=0$ and bounded *above* by $y=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{0}_{a}\\le y\\le \\underbrace{2}_{b}.\n$$\n\nSo, statement “$a=-1$ and $b=1$” is false.\n\nFinally, the correct answer is “${g}_{1}(y)=-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$ and ${g}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ab2b92-956a-5542-8558-9d8353d363f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450060} {:answer/id #uuid "eca73180-f340-5ba3-8d1c-1ba3a952c9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eca73180-f340-5ba3-8d1c-1ba3a952c9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450061} :answer-field/id #uuid "b102cea3-f562-5bbc-b248-b7fd89563d70" :answer-field/key "The zero matrix $O=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $G.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2924e9da-5763-50eb-bf48-93b44a58eaf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450062} {:answer/id #uuid "25d328db-2634-516f-9952-32935f11ffe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25d328db-2634-516f-9952-32935f11ffe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450063} :answer-field/id #uuid "334fb609-34b8-512d-927b-a8ea1e632a29" :answer-field/key "For the zero matrix $O$ and any $A\\in G,$ we have $A-O=A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450985} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "768efe7b-ef20-53e5-a58a-44ad13d32eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450064} {:answer/id #uuid "381ee2c7-9797-5969-a87b-fe851ec6009e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "768efe7b-ef20-53e5-a58a-44ad13d32eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450064} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee93e453-3d49-54de-9414-b1ecee02547b" :answer-field/key "For any $A,B\\in G,$ we have $A-B=B-A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ab2ad7f-5552-5a07-8645-8d079346b7d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162620" :question/problem "Let $G$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{bmatrix},$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The zero matrix $O=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $G.$” is true. Indeed,$O=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{bmatrix}$ with $a=b=0.$\n\n- Statement “For the zero matrix $O$ and any $A\\in G,$ we have $A-O=A.$” is true. Indeed, as for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ with real entries, we have\n\n$$\nA-O=A+(-O)=A+O=A.\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $A,B\\in G,$ we have $A-B=B-A.$” is false. For example, let's consider the matrices $O=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${I}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Then $O$ and ${I}_{2}$ belong to $G,$ and we\nhave \n\n$$\n{I}_{2}-O={I}_{2}\n$$\n\n \nbut \n\n$$\nO-{I}_{2}=-{I}_{2}\\ne {I}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The zero matrix $O=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $G.$”; “For the zero matrix $O$ and any $A\\in G,$ we have $A-O=A.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e2779fb-9930-5fcd-bcd1-7e1f1104d4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450066} {:answer/id #uuid "91b3e3fc-389a-585f-96b5-7db78750f42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91b3e3fc-389a-585f-96b5-7db78750f42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450067} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7c9859-71fa-5115-a310-1182f4bf63bc" :answer-field/key "There is a function $f(x)\\in Q,$ such that $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450987} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "662847ba-aeb6-5cbd-8649-2265e32224d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450068} {:answer/id #uuid "bf79e41d-5399-5862-8d64-f981b0f2cf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf79e41d-5399-5862-8d64-f981b0f2cf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450069} :answer-field/id #uuid "b083e9d7-fb4e-5c84-9a1a-a1c99a0f9d6c" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450988} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69cd0a9e-9920-5b05-8ece-dcad3cae55ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450070} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7468af-0186-5e65-ab49-7c01cd3fc068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc7468af-0186-5e65-ab49-7c01cd3fc068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450071} :answer-field/id #uuid "b050593e-e59b-5bdf-835e-4f773eafb358" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))$ $=\\alpha f(x)$ $+\\alpha g(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff69a5c1-505a-5719-b6b9-7ec69e0931ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-162664" :question/problem "Let $Q$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “There is a function $f(x)\\in Q,$ such that $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$” is true. Consider the null function $f(x)=0=0{x}^{2}\\in Q.$ Then,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot f(x)=(-1)\\cdot 0=0=f(x).\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any function $f(x)\\in Q$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))$ $=\\alpha f(x)$ $+\\alpha g(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “There is a function $f(x)\\in Q,$ such that $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$”; “For any $f(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$”; “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))$ $=\\alpha f(x)$ $+\\alpha g(x).$”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6dc2795-4ab0-51de-a770-20d43c3a88f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450072} {:answer/id #uuid "06198632-4bef-5852-8df3-61b23cc71b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6dc2795-4ab0-51de-a770-20d43c3a88f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450072} :answer-field/id #uuid "76c5b6a9-c201-5cfe-94b7-0a5d6e2baf31" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\in S$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "554b7f4f-d75d-532f-af10-b13a3597fa28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450074} {:answer/id #uuid "39d14144-cd01-511c-b559-2f430b3240b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39d14144-cd01-511c-b559-2f430b3240b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450075} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc461b09-0b94-5bf1-9079-3927e7dcb562" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x)\\in S,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot p(x)\\in S$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5a4b91-36ef-5113-a4b9-d1f9b7d8da80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450076} {:answer/id #uuid "aa572e6a-aad9-513a-b665-99a85554378d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa572e6a-aad9-513a-b665-99a85554378d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450077} :answer-field/id #uuid "55832c01-3fed-5f96-9d33-cae8fdc270f3" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x),q(x)\\in S$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))$ $=\\alpha p(x)$ $-\\alpha q(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69e25145-91f1-58d1-afd8-be54a0c5863e" :question/math-academy-id "q-162665" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is at most $2.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\in S$ is false. The set $S$ contains only polynomials whose degree is at most $2.$ However, $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is *not* a polynomial. So, $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x)\\in S,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot p(x)\\in S$” is true. Let $deg(q)$ the degree of a polynomial $q.$ Then, for any $p(x)\\in S$ we have that $(-1)\\cdot p(x)$ is also a polynomial, and that\n\n$$\ndeg((-1)\\cdot p)=deg(-1)+deg(p)=0+deg(p)\\le 2.\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)p(x)\\in S.$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x),q(x)\\in S$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))$ $=\\alpha p(x)$ $-\\alpha q(x)$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x),q(x)\\in S$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the values $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))=\\alpha p(x)-\\alpha q(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $p(x)\\in S,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot p(x)\\in S$”; “For any $p(x),q(x)\\in S$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))$ $=\\alpha p(x)$ $-\\alpha q(x)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c42ccdb6-b921-5da6-8d61-829338f9c0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450078} {:answer/id #uuid "2b082b3a-de73-5d72-8407-3ea0f366430e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b082b3a-de73-5d72-8407-3ea0f366430e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450079} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ded1d6-fd62-535d-a00c-5652c123a362" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in Y,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A=-A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b94594f5-40c0-57fa-a320-b6e74879d268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450080} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a33687-ca33-58d2-9263-d09f15df4540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a33687-ca33-58d2-9263-d09f15df4540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450081} :answer-field/id #uuid "e22d5ab6-389d-5f69-99dc-1d75e06d9f38" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in Y$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45057e96-393e-5a76-b084-845e711d890f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450082} {:answer/id #uuid "be6cad6a-51eb-557f-9298-7fa92791e5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45057e96-393e-5a76-b084-845e711d890f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450082} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f084e17-158e-5d0d-b97b-c2a08151797a" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in Y$ we have $2A\\in Y.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2124447c-ee22-58ee-9afe-87a9532907c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162668" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices with determinant $1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in Y,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A=-A.$” is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in Y,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, we have\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot {a}_{ij}=-{a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot A=-A.\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in Y$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$” is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in Y,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta ){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\beta {a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in Y$ we have $2A\\in Y.$” is false. For example, the identity matrix ${I}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\in Y,$ however $2{I}_{2}\\notin Y$ because\n\n$$\n|2{I}_{2}|=|2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}|=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $A\\in Y,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A=-A.$”; “For any $A\\in Y$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc10e234-82ec-548f-b508-b8a34d60de48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465477} {:answer/id #uuid "19cc9d63-26ae-5d67-8d2e-92a25b620c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19cc9d63-26ae-5d67-8d2e-92a25b620c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465478} :answer-field/id #uuid "76684f2a-492a-5359-ab60-ed33c7131dda" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d585690c-260f-5e71-a6e3-572e7e3486d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465479} {:answer/id #uuid "2dfff1c9-8854-533f-bcbe-5d8a3b55044b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d585690c-260f-5e71-a6e3-572e7e3486d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465479} :answer-field/id #uuid "d16a6f9f-f813-5bc0-8804-79ea114f5d79" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "934f59a6-e3f6-570b-9a54-e524e4c540a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465481} {:answer/id #uuid "abb738ed-ecd8-58af-9c55-39b58795284c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "934f59a6-e3f6-570b-9a54-e524e4c540a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465481} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec28cbc6-2271-5aa3-a1c8-3a8a32cf506a" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5dd282b-2dab-5297-89c3-a4849921b265" :question/math-academy-id "q-162746" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.06$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.5$ | $0.24$ | $0.06$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ | |  | | $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |  |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ |  |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=1)=f(1,1)=0.06.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.2\\cdot 0.3=0.06.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0) & =0.1\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b6d959-ee25-5492-981c-35d8db8e5d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465483} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9adef5-225c-5e47-85de-42b3cd7836b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06b6d959-ee25-5492-981c-35d8db8e5d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465483} :answer-field/id #uuid "14307e24-b8d0-5de1-9104-6c06ac0c93ca" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=0)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "655fd2b1-caba-581e-9f02-5af690a77b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465485} {:answer/id #uuid "68af336e-64bf-56bf-84dd-85cd858cec6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "655fd2b1-caba-581e-9f02-5af690a77b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465485} :answer-field/id #uuid "d37345fc-3288-5bfa-8a83-9ad74cabae6f" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f3db53-a644-5ca7-a50d-da78184c6ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465487} {:answer/id #uuid "10595161-cfd2-59f2-802a-94f7478661b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7f3db53-a644-5ca7-a50d-da78184c6ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465487} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bf4bd53-b362-55cb-86c6-31f5ad34dba8" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "745e2846-c808-51fa-a431-23f636897e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-162824" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | |  | | $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=1,Y=0)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=0)=f(1,0)=0.25.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0)=0.5\\cdot 0.6=0.3.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=1,Y=0)\\ne P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6bd5f7b-86e2-5e7e-b73c-315158951242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465489} {:answer/id #uuid "69898b06-6833-5e82-bda7-be2ba91dcd05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69898b06-6833-5e82-bda7-be2ba91dcd05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465490} :answer-field/id #uuid "64426418-f534-5933-9f46-35719ecf03ce" :answer-field/key "$P(X=0,Y=-2)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dece8f5a-d33c-55b1-8727-78b35148f159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465491} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0e11ca-3eba-54ba-b933-6364f809561b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a0e11ca-3eba-54ba-b933-6364f809561b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465492} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a934dbd-cdc8-57f7-8678-a94b82ca59cf" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11b7752-cf12-5634-a8c7-a28b035c3ce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465493} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8854e9-a444-5ea2-b47b-67f40c37002e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d8854e9-a444-5ea2-b47b-67f40c37002e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465494} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ef4a0e-65a8-501a-9a5a-8c9657c7647e" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b24b5d8-591a-5107-953f-3194f9f2c074" :question/math-academy-id "q-163605" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{12}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{24}$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{2}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{3}{8}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{5}{8}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=0,Y=-2)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=-2)=f(0,-2)=\\frac{1}{4}.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,2) & =\\frac{5}{12}=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,-2) & =\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,2) & =\\frac{5}{24}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is true. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=0,Y=-2)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$; “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$”; “$X$ and $Y$ are independent”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a8ad20-3764-5670-8078-71b7721fc577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465495} {:answer/id #uuid "27b99241-25ca-5909-922e-fe366e5d4927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27b99241-25ca-5909-922e-fe366e5d4927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465496} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa1944d-ce09-51f9-8a91-e6875021ae04" :answer-field/key "$P(X=8,Y=1)$ $=P(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d4f6faf-e175-54c4-a961-1ff23aedd8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465497} {:answer/id #uuid "057dab26-bc3c-5bcc-81b6-1a2bb82c5a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "057dab26-bc3c-5bcc-81b6-1a2bb82c5a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465498} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e7a4211-9bc2-523c-9177-898dbab2152d" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d6ce853-4f78-5f21-87d1-1b375cb77cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465499} {:answer/id #uuid "0da85821-e95e-5859-8a01-ba978cb19b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0da85821-e95e-5859-8a01-ba978cb19b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465500} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a10f283-8c48-5c9d-a0f4-a9c8b4e9c55e" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25bf9bc6-630d-50c0-9382-20c9fae3e81f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163617" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $0.22$ | $0.33$ |\n| $X=8$ | $0.18$ | $0.27$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $3$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | |  | | $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | $8$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=8,Y=1)$ $=P(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=8,Y=1)=f(8,1)=0.27.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(8)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.45\\cdot 0.6=0.27.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,-1) & =0.22=0.55\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-1) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,1) & =0.33=0.55\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(8,-1) & =0.18=0.45\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(8)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-1) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is true. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=8,Y=1)$ $=P(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)$; “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$”; “$X$ and $Y$ are independent”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284418 